  "hindi": "हे बलवान् अग्नि, तुम्हारा मुख भद्र है; वह सूर्य के पास चमकता है। चमकता हुआ, देखने के लिए, रात में भी दिखाई देता है, अशुष्क; देखने के लिए, रूप में, अन्न।",
  "english": "Good is your face, O mighty Agni; it shines near the sun. Bright, to be seen, it is seen even by night, not parched; for sight, in form, food.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Line b is obscure to me and is translated only literally. arūkṣitam (cidarūkṣitam = cit arūkṣitam) is read as \"not parched\" and I do not know which noun it qualifies; annam and the phrase dṛśe ā rūpe are not tied together by any verb. In line a, upāke with the genitive sūryasya is read as \"near the sun\" (it could also be read \"near, of the sun\" as a possessive sense). sahasin \"mighty\" (voc.).",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
