  "hindi": "हे अग्नि, गाने वाले के लिए प्रेरित विचार को पार करो, खुले स्थान को, कम्पन के साथ स्तुति पाते हुए, हे बलवान् जन्म वाले। जो तुमने सब देवों के साथ जीता है, हे दीप्तिमान्, वह हमें दो, हे अत्यन्त महान्, प्रचुर स्तोत्र।",
  "english": "Overcome, O Agni, for the singer the inspired thought, the opening, being praised with trembling, O strong-born one. What you have won with all the gods, O bright one, that give us, O very great one, abundant hymns.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Line a is unclear to me. vi ṣāhi is read as a form of vi-√sah (\"overcome\"), but other analyses (vi-√sā, \"release, open\") are possible, and the objects manīṣām and kham are not tied together by any clear construction. vepasā \"with trembling\" (excitement). In line b the pf. vāvanaḥ is read as 2 sg. \"you have won\"; manma (n. pl.) is \"hymns\" (manman).",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
