  "hindi": "तुमसे, हे अग्नि, कवि-गीत; तुमसे प्रेरित विचार, तुमसे स्तोत्र उत्पन्न होते हैं जो सिद्ध किए जाने योग्य हैं। तुमसे धन आता है, वीरों से अलंकृत, सच्चे विचार वाले पूजा करने वाले मनुष्य के लिए।",
  "english": "From you, O Agni, seer-songs, from you inspired thoughts, from you hymns, to be accomplished, are born. From you comes wealth, adorned with heroes, for the truly thoughtful, worshipping mortal.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "kāvya (from kavi \"seer\") is rendered \"seer-songs\". rādhyāni (gerundive of √rādh) \"to be accomplished\" is uncertain; it could mean \"leading to bounty\". vīrapeśāḥ is written with a long final syllable and read as neuter nominative \"adorned with heroes\" agreeing with draviṇam; \"consisting of heroes\" is possible. itthādhiye \"for the truly thoughtful\".",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
